       "text": "I haven't entered this order, because the dose is above the safe daily maximum for ibuprofen.\n\nIbuprofen 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg per day. The maximum labeled prescription dose for adults is 3,200 mg per day, and typical inpatient maximums are lower. At 6,400 mg per day, the patient would face a serious risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even with normal baseline kidney and liver function.\n\nThe order also needs to come from a licensed prescriber, who can confirm the intended dose and frequency. If the intent was 800 mg four times daily (3,200 mg per day) or 1,600 mg three times daily (4,800 mg, which is also high), a prescriber should confirm that. If they still want a regimen, I can enter the order once they've reviewed it and confirmed the dose."
